            "review_title": "Review at Restaurant Ai Hue 2",
            "review_text": "Vince Huynh\nLondon, United Kingdom177 contributions\n0\nVery tasty Dim Sum, good value for money and excellent service\nApr 2018 • Friends\nThis is well know restaurant and we was there for breakfast Dim Sum, the dishes tasty and follow Hong Kong style Dim Sum, good selection of Dim Sum and so the price which very affordable for the quality of the food. I would happy recommend the Prawn wrapped in fried tofu skin (I don't really like tofu but this dishe is yummy) and so Har Gow and the Kim Sa Bun (which I could happily eat three of them in one go)\nThe atmosphere was a bit noisy as always in a Chinese restaurant but acceptable as few big tables of large group near us. Service was quick and promptly and the serving staff well informed us of the favourite dishes which I glad we ordered it base on her recommended. Head of Dim Sum chef Mr Quan also chosen some of his recommend dish (which included the Prawn wrapped in tofu skin)\nFor mid end casual Dim Sum in Saigon, I would happy to recommend this restaurant any time. Dim Sum is for breakfast so come in morning 😊\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 10, 2018",
