            "review_text": "Daty L\n74 contributions\n0\nMid-end Chinese food restaurant\nJan 2018\nWell, you shall rarely disappointed about Chinese food, especially with Vietnamese fusion taste. I have been here number of times and enjoyed very much. The food is amazing, typical Hong Kong style with Vietnamese flavors (I guess). You can try out fried prawn dim with mayonnaise sauce (my favorite), Perking style roasted duck is good too. The price is not too high but not cheap at all. Staff is helpful and attentive. The minus point is the location of the restaurant is on a quite small street, that's quite struggle for those who come there with family by car. Anyway, recommend this restaurant for family dinner.\nRead more\nWritten April 3, 2018",
