            "review_text": "ngoctrantran\nSan Jose, California315 contributions\n0\nMeh!\nJan 2018 • Family\nWe are in VN so we’ll spend our VND accordingly to the VN standard. At this premium price, I expect most of what I order to be above average to earn solid stars. Shanghai dumplings have been my favorite dumplings of all. Ai Hue Shanghai has lots of broth inside, the skin is thin, but it is doughy in texture. Not great, but not bad. My Husband’s favorite dumpling is Xiu Mai. Ai Hue Xiu Mai doesn’t have enough shrimp so it lacks crunchiness. The steamed rice roll, AKA Bánh cuốn, is slightly mushy, lacking the slight chewy springy texture of a great Bánh cuon. The rest of dim sum are not bad, but not great either. Ai Hue best is their desserts. The egg tarts, especially the one with salted egg, and the fried rice balls, especially the bitter melon, are spot on delicious.\nRead more\nWritten January 19, 2018",
