            "review_text": "Davidsworld\n24 contributions\n0\nGood Chinese style dim sum\nOct 2017 • Family\nQuality: 3\nDecor: 4\nPresentation: 3\nService: 5\nPrice: $$$$\n\nNice Chinese restaurant in the Chinatown area of Ho Chi Minh. If you want dim sum, don't confuse this place with the other... they have two locations. The other one does not serve dim sum. The restaurant has been around for decades and continues to look good. The food quality is average in comparison to dim sum I've tasted from different countries. For the price you're paying... it's definitely not worth it. Mind you, I am referring to people paying in CAD or USD. And definitely very expensive for the locals. The service, well, they're impeccable as they are constantly attending to your needs from tea refilling to immediate empty dish removals... well they do have two bodies standing there to wait on you afterall 😉\nOverall, if you're a visitor to the Chinatown area, it's worth a visit and check it out. Other than that, if you're looking for taste and quality, maybe it's not worth your time. 4 stars! Service and nice decor pushed it up from what would've been 3 stars.\nRead more\nWritten October 14, 2017",
